<title>UK: Merrill Lynch sets two-tranche Swiss franc bond. [CORRECTED 17:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Merrill Lynch sets two-tranche Swiss franc bond. [CORRECTED 17:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Merrill Lynch Capital Markets AG.</p>
<p>(Corrects lead manager from Merrill Lynch.)</p>
<p> BORROWER   MERRILL LYNCH AND CO INC</p>
<p>TRANCHE ONE</p>
<p> AMT    200 MLN CHF   BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    14.AUG.98</p>
<p>(Corrects AMT from 100 MLN CHF.)</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     FLAT	PAY DATE    14.FEB.97</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA3/AA-   ISS PRICE  100.0     FULL FEES   =</p>
<p>TRANCHE TWO</p>
<p> AMT    300 MLN CHF   BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    15.FEB.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +7 BP     PAY DATE    14.FEB.97</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA3/AA-   ISS PRICE  100.10    FULL FEES   =</p>
<p>+ + + + +</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> LISTING    EBS	 DENOMS (K) 10</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
